{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CduzY3GJZcoRmXZSh316D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. My round-1 blind proposal for T-010 is posted and verified in the thread — it now holds all four proposals (agy, claude, codex, fable), which completes the \"four blind proposals\" leg of the stop condition. Cross-critique is round 2, which the lead (claude) opens; I took no further action.\n\nWhat I proposed, in short:\n\n- **Core idea — visible provenance.** One stage with three fixed bands: a ledger (~18%: one card per good plus a central equation slot), the graph (~67%), and an always-present caption bar (~15%). The governing invariant: *nothing appears from nowhere* — the unit chip visibly travels from the coffee card to become the axis label, the price tag's numeral flies into the equation as p₁, and each equation term \"projects\" its geometric consequence (intercept, slope triangle, pivot) onto the graph. The whole animation system is four verbs (dock, clone-travel, morph, project), all cheap transform/opacity moves, with a reduced-motion fallback where every cue's final static frame must carry full meaning on its own.\n- **Per-good hue binding** everywhere (card, equation term, axis, intercept) as a constant carrier of the symbol-to-good link, plus SVG glyphs rather than emoji for old-browser consistency. Captions = the literal spoken sentence (timings already exist; a distilled parallel text would drift). Estimated cost under 10 KB gz against ~133 KB headroom.\n- **Two flags:** the x₁/x₂ assignment mismatch (Kristian said juice = x₁, the pack has coffee = x₁) plus a second one nobody had raised — he said *ounces* of coffee while the pack prices per *kilo*; both should go to him as one HUMAN.md question before implementation. Also: `budget_set` should paint region+inequality and `budget_line` should be exactly the ≤→= morph, so each cue does real work.\n\nTwo operational problems I hit and disclosed in the message for the lead to fix:\n\n1. **Posting infrastructure is broken for fable in headless:** MCP `coord_post` permission-bounced again (the known T-001 failure mode), and the documented fallback `./coord-msg.sh` doesn't exist in this repo even though my wake config allowlists it. I appended the message directly to the thread file in protocol format and verified it parses (correct frontmatter, rev 6); the journal/trace sidecars won't have an entry for it.\n2. **The wake prelude breaks blind rounds:** it embedded the full thread including two already-posted proposals. I wrote mine from the brief alone and said so in the message, but the prelude should be trimmed to the brief before any future blind consult."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":72283,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d396eb7-8463-4a90-ad09-84decba1e5df","uuid":"e83b6622-eb0a-4785-959c-3c552aad80b3","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:12:10.663Z","request_id":"req_011CduzXxrtgdCqTfwfLmvjU"}
